# Publify persists the user display name with no length bound: the
# users.name column is a text type, so a profile edit can store
# megabytes into the name rendered on every page, feed and session the
# user touches (unbounded input to resource exhaustion and cookie
# breakage, CWE-400/CWE-20). The User model in
# publify_core/app/models/user.rb bounds some string attributes -- the
# login to 3..40, and email and text_filter_name to 255 through the
# StringLengthLimit concern's validates_default_string_length -- while
# the name attribute appears in no validation at all; it is read back
# by display_name. Pool commit 29a5837c29 is the real fix (the advisory
# links this exact commit, "Validate length of user's name attribute"):
# `validates :name, length: { maximum: 2048 }` -- generous for any real
# name, bounded for the column semantics. No pool correction.
#
# Held ATTENTION, model-level length budgets, rechecked at the span
# tip. Fresh scans of the real checkout at both revisions (3 x
# --cache off each, timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB) report the identical
# 75-finding set: the single finding in user.rb is VYQL-CRY-001 on the
# SHA1 password digest, which shifts user.rb:81 -> :82 with the added
# line, and nothing in the findings or match view touches the
# validation surface -- no later-shipped rule fires and no existing
# detection was missed. The discriminating fact spans three files: the
# controller's mass-assignment list (admin/users_controller.rb
# user_params permits :name among 25 symbols), the schema column
# (db/schema.rb declares users.name as t.text, no limit), and the
# model's validation set. Presence bindings are lexically confined, so
# no binding sees the three together, and the Ruby frontend emits no
# call-argument tokens at all (the context walk produces assign:,
# selector:, expr:, field:, call_path:, call:, index:, literal:,
# interpolation: and regex: tokens only, and a bare symbol argument
# produces no token), so even the in-file pairing "which attributes
# does this validates call bound" is unavailable. A class-level
# negation ("the model carries no length validation") is satisfied by
# neither revision -- the vulnerable model already bounds login, email
# and text_filter_name, and the parent commit is itself a
# length-hardening pass -- so it never fires here. An attribute-level
# verdict is unshippably broad: the same permit list still writes
# description, url, msn, aim, yahoo, jabber, twitter, firstname,
# lastname and nickname into the unbounded serialized settings column
# at the fixed revision, and unbounded text is the norm for legitimate
# fields (an article body must not be capped at 2048), the same
# measured family as a request-body byte cap and a model write with no
# ownership key. The bound itself is arbitrary -- "generous for any
# real name" -- so no vocabulary states what the budget should be;
# only column semantics and feature intent know, and neither is in
# code the scanner sees. Keying on :name or on Publify's own
# validates_default_string_length DSL detects this application rather
# than the weakness. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry -- the engine mishandles
# no construct here; the blocker is cross-file expressibility plus
# verdict precision. No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1615
# pins both revisions on the real file shape, both rejecting
# VYQL-DOS-029: when attribute-budget vocabulary lands, the
# unvalidated form must flip to expect.

test "rank1615: the display name appears in no length validation"
  lang ruby
  file publify_core/app/models/user.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class User < ApplicationRecord
    devise :database_authenticatable, :registerable,
           :recoverable, :rememberable, :trackable, :validatable
    include StringLengthLimit

    before_validation :set_default_profile

    validates :login, uniqueness: true
    validates :email, :login, presence: true
    validates :login, length: { in: 3..40 }
    validates_default_string_length :email, :text_filter_name

    belongs_to :resource, optional: true
    has_many :articles

    def display_name
      if nickname.present?
        nickname
      elsif name.present?
        name
      else
        login
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1615: the fixed revision bounds the name length"
  lang ruby
  file publify_core/app/models/user.rb
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class User < ApplicationRecord
    devise :database_authenticatable, :registerable,
           :recoverable, :rememberable, :trackable, :validatable
    include StringLengthLimit

    before_validation :set_default_profile

    validates :login, uniqueness: true
    validates :email, :login, presence: true
    validates :login, length: { in: 3..40 }
    validates_default_string_length :email, :text_filter_name
    validates :name, length: { maximum: 2048 }

    belongs_to :resource, optional: true
    has_many :articles

    def display_name
      if nickname.present?
        nickname
      elsif name.present?
        name
      else
        login
      end
    end
  end
  ```
